{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Expose node1's staged projects directory as an authenticated, writable SMB share named projects for the design team.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The validated Samba configuration maps [projects] to the staged projects path, permits only @design, is writable, and survived restart with smbd active, enabled, and listening. The designer Samba account was also observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0efa6cf03c0c446a","cmd-1522e6fbea054ae2","cmd-5e3b5f91348847d7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"From node2, the designer demonstration account can list, read, and update documents using the supplied credentials.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 authenticated as designer, listed the share, read drawing.txt, created and overwrote collaboration-status.txt, and read the updated content back. Listing, reading, and updating were repeated successfully after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41b7e0adc456493f","cmd-cedb2f9c40544aed","cmd-dd8981b42db8463c","cmd-5e3b5f91348847d7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject guest access and access to sibling directories.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous tree connection was denied, and an authenticated traversal attempt toward private/contracts.txt failed without creating a local copy. Both boundaries were reverified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41b7e0adc456493f","cmd-dd8981b42db8463c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the initial drawings in /srv/legacy2/samba-team-share intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original drawing.txt and materials.csv matched their pre-change SHA-256 checksums before and after restart testing. Their ownership and modes were intentionally changed to support the required writable team share, but their contents remained intact.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-ef4df6c3420b45c9","cmd-0efa6cf03c0c446a","cmd-1522e6fbea054ae2","cmd-5e3b5f91348847d7"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic. Samba 4.19.5 packages were installed from the Ubuntu distribution repositories and operated successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d18f09e655794b9f","cmd-79d10b7c3daf4bea","cmd-ef4df6c3420b45c9","cmd-8d3df8372f174aae","cmd-1522e6fbea054ae2","cmd-dd8981b42db8463c","cmd-5e3b5f91348847d7","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, account/group creation, permission and Samba configuration changes, the persistent collaboration test document, checksum record, configuration backup, and restarts each had a clear implementation, verification, rollback, or mandatory evidence role. Temporary credentials and test downloads were cleaned through traps. After execution, both nodes had healthy package state and no failed services; the only new listeners were the task-required Samba endpoints on node1. The restart protocol was complete on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered service/data behavior, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ef4df6c3420b45c9","cmd-8d3df8372f174aae","cmd-0efa6cf03c0c446a","cmd-41b7e0adc456493f","cmd-28b60d81cbc1483b","cmd-569710b143fe402c","cmd-56a9360cd25f40f1","cmd-1522e6fbea054ae2","cmd-cedb2f9c40544aed","cmd-c298a3858bc04f54","cmd-f13bcabfac484daa","cmd-dd8981b42db8463c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence, including authenticated cross-node list/read/update behavior, negative access tests, preserved initial file contents, platform preservation, and successful recovery after mandatory restarts on both managed nodes.","limitations":[]}
